00:35:43.320 --> 00:35:46.476
and Bob Boice on scheduling
writing sessions.

00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:47.834
And thanks to Candice Faktor

00:35:47.858 --> 00:35:50.886
for the amazing introduction
to Margaret Atwood.

00:35:50.910 --> 00:35:54.449
(Music)

00:35:55.611 --> 00:35:57.666
MA: OK, so here's the story.

00:35:57.690 --> 00:36:00.326
We were throwing a party
at our house for some writers.

00:36:00.350 --> 00:36:02.255
And there they were, all milling around.

00:36:02.279 --> 00:36:06.016
And then this young woman,
who was about 35,

00:36:06.040 --> 00:36:08.396
said she was having a heart attack.

00:36:08.420 --> 00:36:11.914
Then I called 911
and the paramedics arrived,

00:36:11.938 --> 00:36:14.166
lumpety-bump up the steps.

00:36:14.190 --> 00:36:16.586
I love paramedics.

00:36:16.610 --> 00:36:19.896
So in they come,
and here's the conversation.

00:36:19.920 --> 00:36:22.817
First paramedic:
"Do you know whose house this is?"

00:36:22.841 --> 00:36:25.416
Second paramedic: "No, whose house is it?"

00:36:25.440 --> 00:36:26.946
First paramedic:

00:36:26.970 --> 00:36:28.766
"It's Margaret Atwood's house."

00:36:28.790 --> 00:36:30.146
Second paramedic:

00:36:30.170 --> 00:36:32.215
"Margaret Atwood? Is she still alive?"

00:36:32.239 --> 00:36:33.756
(Adam laughs)

